Abstract: We propose <code>&#91;&#91;@expression]]</code> for compile-time decorators, with each returned definition passed to the next decorator.
Abstract:
Abstract: Each decorator call must be a constant expression. Decorators can validate or transform class or function definitions and store computed annotations even if nobody queries them. These annotations can retain facts about intermediate definitions for later reflection. The examples require new language and library support. How definitions are represented, when replacement occurs, and which reflected entities retain their identity remain unresolved. We request direction on this application and composition model.
